Hi jbikker / tinybvh team!

I have an issue when trying to use GLM with TinyBVH; the linked blog post (or rather, the blog post that linked me to this repo) states that you can use GLM with this library, but it's giving me compile errors. I'm assuming that, since the blog states that you can use GLM, it should be possible. I have the following code at the top of my main file:

```cpp
#define TINYBVH_IMPLEMENTATION
#define TINYBVH_USE_CUSTOM_VECTOR_TYPES
#define NO_CUSTOM_GEOMETRY // Only triangles
#define NO_DOUBLE_PRECISION_SUPPORT // Only floats

namespace tinybvh {
  using bvhint2 = glm::ivec2;
  using bvhint3 = glm::ivec3;
  using bvhuint2 = glm::uvec2;
  using bvhvec2 = glm::vec2;
  using bvhvec3 = glm::vec3;
  using bvhvec4 = glm::vec4;
  using bvhdbl3 = glm::dvec3;
  using bvhmat4 = glm::mat4;
}

#include "tiny_bvh.h"
```

However, I'm getting a lot of errors relating to these `using bvh___ = glm::___` types when I try to compile. A tiny subset of this:

```
In file included from /home/taylor/programming/ray-tracer/main.cpp:26:
