 2350 |                         for (uint32_t a = 0; a < 3; a++) for (uint32_t i = 0; i < BVHBINS; i++) binMin[a][i] = BVH_FAR, binMax[a][i] = -BVH_FAR;
      |                                                                                                                ^~~~~~~
/usr/include/glm/detail/type_vec3.hpp:176:59: note: candidate: ‘constexpr glm::vec<3, T, Q>& glm::vec<3, T, Q>::operator=(const glm::vec<3, T, Q>&) [with T = float; glm::qualifier Q = glm::packed_highp]’
  176 |                 GLM_FUNC_DECL GLM_CONSTEXPR vec<3, T, Q>& operator=(vec<3, T, Q> const& v) GLM_DEFAULT;
      |                                                           ^~~~~~~~
```

(note that these errors are the first ones that occurred as well)

I'm wondering if these types of errors are known, and whether I'm just doing something wrong. It's been a while since I did anything with C++ or GLM, so I might very well be :) It seems like the issues mostly happen due to the GLM templates and/or GLM vectors not having a constructor / operator= for assigning with scalars?

Just in case it's important: I have taken the `tiny_bvh.h` file from master a few hours ago, and I have glm 0.9.9.8+ds-7 (as installed by `sudo apt install libglm-dev` on Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS).

I look forward to hearing from you! If GLM doesn't work, it's not a dealbreaker for me, but I would like to hear what you suggest as an alternative!

