The temp alloc is bump/arena allocator, but it will allocate more blocks if needed, each the same size. If you ask 100MB, though, it will create one block that size. it is generally meant for bunch of small-ish temporary allocations.

In the example, the temp alloc grows up to 3.5MB on highest zoom level. I'm limiting the max font size to 256 (actual image is slightly larger). Summa summarum, 512k or 1M is probably good starting point, it's not a hard limit. "}, {'user': 'ApoorvaJ', 'created_at': '2025-06-09T16:20:21Z', 'body': "Ah, I didn't realize that it will allocate more blocks if needed, because I'm getting a reliable crash in my code if I allocate too little memory. I haven't fully narrowed it down, but here's the error message:

